# The resumable name store the corpus builder walks the registry into: one
# line per package name, around ninety megabytes at full size. It is an
# intermediate, not an artifact.
.corpus-work/

# A built corpus. Ten megabytes of generated data whose provenance is a
# dated registry walk -- it belongs to a release, not to a commit.
packages/core/data/

# The private dogfood tier: the list of local repositories to scan, and
# anything a run writes about them. The harness only ever emits counts, but
# the list itself names paths, so it stays out of the repository.
bench/repos.local.json
bench/baseline.local.json
bench/results.local.json

# The umbrella's hook manifest. It records absolute paths on the machine that
# ran init, so it belongs to that machine rather than to a commit. The policy
# file beside it, .guardrails.yaml, is tracked: it is the configuration CI
# reads, and a gate policy nobody can review is not a policy.
.guardrails/
